   MONTENEGRO, JUN 10-14, 2025},
Abstract = {The Internet of Things is envisioned to enhance connectivity and expand
   its application to several domains. IoT is currently well advanced,
   characterized by the increasingly prevalent deployment of interconnected
   devices. The perception layer of IoT encompasses a comprehensive
   integration of sensors, hardware, software, compilers, and benchmarks,
   facilitating seamless communication and data exchange across various
   devices. The paper sheds light on the popular Software, Compilers and
   Benchmarks used in embedded devices in an IoT scenario. The paper
   extensively reviews the latest and most prevalent commercial and
   research products among these components. A summary of characteristics,
   cost and their capabilities are discussed. With this review we aim to
   offer valuable insights for optimizing performance and efficiency in
   embedded systems, thereby guiding future advancements in the field.},
