   02, 2025},
Abstract = {The advent of Machine Learning (ML) and Reinforcement Learning (RL)
   augmented macro placement techniques have shown to improve key design
   metrics on synthetic designs, within a few hours. This ML-driven
   approach to a traditionally iterative process typically spanning
   multiple weeks has architected an industrial mindset change towards
   automated macro placement. However, can the techniques replicate the
   impressive results on real-world designs, thereby bridging the gap
   between research and industry? This paper explores the answer to the
   above question by experimenting with ML-driven macro placement
   techniques from a leading external EDA tool on industry leading GPU
   designs. We define the bounding scope, document the process, publish the
   results, and analyze the experiments to provide an industrial
   perspective to the existing ML-macro placement methods. This industrial
   perspective forms the crux of this paper detailing the different
   implementation challenges and providing recommendations so that existing
   ML-methods can be fine-tuned to bridge the gap between research and
   industry needs.},
