Year = {2025},
Pages = {120-124},
Note = {7th International Conference on Artificial Intelligence Circuits and
   Systems-AICAS-Annual, Bordeaux, FRANCE, APR 28-30, 2025},
Abstract = {For a long time, DNN inference has played a huge role in many
   device-edge scenarios. However, due to a lack of training capabilities,
   it often needs to be trained and downloaded in the cloud, which brings
   limitations to deviceedge AI. This article proposes a device-edge DNN
   inference artificial intelligence processor termed UPE (Union Processing
   Element) which supports reconfigurable training offline and has an
   improved solution with three characteristics. Firstly, UPE has a DNN
   Training Inference Reconfigurable Computing (TIRC) architecture, which
   can reconstruct the computing unit from inference to training in real
   time to complete partial weight updates. Secondly, UPE has a Dynamic
   Pruning Optimization Method (DPOM), which supports separately branch
   pruning for different levels of inference and training. Thirdly, UPE
   includes the Flexible Precision Simplified Computing (FPSC) scheme,
   which can compress data where DNN training and numerical format
   inference coexist. Using 28nm CMOS process for evaluation, UPE performs
   well in terms of energy consumption in inference AI processor, which is
   also able to accomplish the training and weights offline self-updating
   in device-edge.},
