   Zaixin and Li, Mo and Zhang, Jian and Chen, Kefan and Chen, Feiliang and
   Huang, Wanxia},
Title = {Optical True Random Number Generator Based on Reconfigurable
   Ge2Sb2Te5 PUFs},
Journal = {ACS PHOTONICS},
Year = {2024},
Volume = {11},
Number = {11},
Pages = {4691-4699},
Month = {OCT 29},
Abstract = {True random number generators (TRNGs) are the fundamental building
   blocks for encryption. Physical unclonable functions (PUFs) prepared
   based on stochastic processes, with the advantages of being impossible
   to imitate and tamper with, are a new source for generating high-quality
   random numbers. However, most proposed PUFs form a fixed structure after
   preparation; the as-generated random number sequence is thus fixed. In
   this article, a reconfigurable optical PUF/TRNG is fabricated by
   utilizing the phase change properties of the disordered Ge2Sb2Te5 (GST)
   nanocrystalline film. By heating and holding the GST film, its
   crystallization ratio can be manipulated, generating multiple sets of
   uncorrelated speckle patterns, which can be converted into multiple
   random arrays by binary digitization. The random array was verified to
   have good randomness by the National Institute of Standards and
   Technology (NIST) randomness test and the DIEHARD(ER) test suites. The
   proposed true random number generator can be used as a secret key to
   complete authentication or encryption with high security and high
   stability.},
Type = {Article},
Affiliation = {Chen, KF; Huang, WX (Corresponding Author), Sichuan Univ, Coll Mat Sci \& Engn, Chengdu 610065, Peoples R China.
