Year = {2024},
Volume = {220},
Month = {NOV 15},
Abstract = {This review study examines the diverse applications of carbon nanotubes
   (CNTs), emphasizing their remarkable characteristics, including their
   cylindrical nanostructure, exceptional mechanical strength, distinctive
   electrical properties, and efficient thermal conductivity. These
   attributes contribute to the versatility of CNTs, enabling their
   utilization across various fields. Within the domain of electronics,
   (CNTs) assume a crucial function in the advancement of high-performance
   field effect transistors (FETs) characterized by diminished dimensions
   and enhanced operational velocities. Concurrently, the incorporation of
   these components into composite materials enhances their mechanical
   strength and improves their ability to control thermal energy. (CNTs)
   have shown significant promise in transforming energy conversion and
   storage technologies, such as batteries and supercapacitors, as well as
   enhancing the performance of photovoltaic cells in solar energy systems.
   Within the field of biomedicine, (CNTs) exhibit considerable potential
   for precise administration of drugs and genes, regenerative medicine
   applications, biosensing capabilities, and bioimaging techniques.
   However, the utilization of CNTs in these areas is not without its
   obstacles, including the need for effective control over their
   chirality, ensuring compatibility with biological systems, and achieving
   scalability in their production. Due to continuous progress in precise
   manufacturing and functionalization methodologies, (CNTs) present viable
   solutions to the aforementioned issues and possess the capacity to
   foster improvements in several technical and medicinal domains.
   Consequently, CNTs have emerged as a captivating field of research and
   inquiry.},
