   Sang-Jae},
Title = {Hybrid triboelectric nanogenerators: Revolutionizing the energy
   harvesting through material diversity and device architecture for
   different applications},
Journal = {NANO ENERGY},
Year = {2024},
Volume = {131},
Number = {A},
Month = {DEC 1},
Abstract = {Triboelectric nanogenerators (TENGs) are transforming energy harvesting
   by cleverly combining them with other energy sources. Hybrid
   triboelectric nanogenerators offer a promising approach to enhance power
   generation by effectively harnessing multiple energy sources. This
   review provides an overview of the different hybrid TENGs, emphasizing
   their ability to integrate various energy harvesting mechanisms, such as
   piezoelectricity, electromagnetic induction, pyroelectric, and
   photovoltaics, with the materials choice, concept of design, and mode of
   operation. By incorporating various energy sources, these nanogenerators
   can function in a wide range of environments, efficiently capturing
   energy from multiple available sources. This integration enhances their
   dependability and self-sufficiency. Through the synergistic combination
   of multiple energy sources, hybrid TENGs demonstrate enhanced power
   generation capabilities when compared to single-source counterparts.
   Apart from that, coupling the field of electronics and photonics with
   the TENG gives new direction and possibilities. The application of the
   different hybrid nanogenerators was detailed. Furthermore, the review
   discusses the challenges and potential future advancements in optimizing
   the efficiency of power generation, scalability, and integration of
   hybrid TENGs.},
